<br/>
The &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; with Wireless Charging Case are the best choice for most buyers. For &#36;20 more than the base model, you get an extra hour of listening time per charge with ANC, volume swipes on the stems, wireless charging, and a speaker that makes a misplaced case easier to find. Choose the &#36;129 model if the lowest price matters most and you are content with its shorter battery life and USB-C-only charging case.<br/>
<br/>
However, the &zwnj;AirPods Pro 3&zwnj; are worth the extra &#36;100 over the higher-end &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; if noise cancellation is your priority and you prefer a snug in-ear fit. Apple says they provide up to three times as much ANC as the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj;, since the ear tips create a physical seal. Their eight-hour listening time per charge is particularly useful on long journeys. In our <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/15/airpods-5-hands-on/">hands-on testing</a>, the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; sounded muddier than the Pro 3, particularly in the lower midrange.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;AirPods Pro 3&zwnj; are also the clear choice if you want their hearing health features or heart rate sensing during workouts without relying on an Apple Watch. Their charging case adds Precision Finding, too. If you dislike silicone ear tips, the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; let you keep the open-ear fit while getting nearly all of the everyday listening features shared by the Pro model.<br/>
